Z||000000||Formula88||11-21-2001||02:32 PM||||Ok, I got the KYB struts on my Formula, but I'm having trouble getting the right rear camber adjusted correctly.  Can anyone with KYB struts on their 88 give me some insight?  Do I need to elongate the adjustment slot for the lower strut bolt?  Do I need a camber kit?  (that's what my alignment shop said).  <P>You can check out everything that's happened so far, and see the spec's I'm getting from this link... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015624.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015624.html</A> <P>Thanks for any help people!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||11-21-2001||04:01 PM||||As I posted before ... you have to grind out the mounting surface that is hitting the top of the knuckle.  Elongating the alignment holes will not help!!!<P>Go back to the original post where I posted the pictures for the small area that needs grinding.<P>BTW, I agree with the other posters about the alignment kit ... it makes the job a lot easier but is NOT needed to do the job and do it right!<P>Paul<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||11-21-2001||04:26 PM||||I'll check your pics in the last post.  I wasn't sure if that would be necessary, since I was able to get them installed without grinding.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||11-21-2001||04:51 PM||||It's a toss up on which '88 Fieros need this "adjustment".  I have only had camber issues on one '88 Fiero with KYB struts and I had the shop (Sears) fix it for me.  All of the other '88 Fieros that I have owned with KYB struts (4 or 5) have not had any problems.....go figure.<P>Anyways.....Paul shows a very nice picture of what needs to be modified in a previous post. <P>Good luck with that shop!   ||||reg||1
