Z||000006||RossT||11-22-2001||10:38 PM||||Thanks Formula88. One more question for you.<BR>I want to put the fierostore gt steering wheel in my formula.  I understand that you have done this.  Exactly what parts are needed to do it.  Horn button and what else?<BR>Thanks for your help.<P>Ross<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||11-22-2001||11:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RossT:<BR><B>I want to put the fierostore gt steering wheel in my formula.  Exactly what parts are needed to do it.  Horn button and what else?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Ross,<P>You will need the contact parts (along with the GT horn button) to make it work.  It includes a small spring and a black plastic thing that holds a small metal rod.....it is this rod that makes contact with the horn button and makes the horn work.<P>I have a few of these lying around so e-mail me your mailing address and I'll send a "kit" to you.<P>   <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||11-23-2001||12:13 AM||||Actually, I haven't.  My car has a factory GT steering wheel in it, not the repro, and it was in the car when I bought it.  Can't help you there.  I will likely be putting in their repro in the future, though, as my leather on the top of the wheel is coming loose.<P>With the standard Pegasus horn button instead of the GT emblem button, it looks like it belongs there.  I much prefer the 3 spoke of the 4 spoke.||||reg||1
